WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.590
The Monday at eight vector has
four active raw indicators.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.900
Training standardization maps the hour
eight entry to about four point seven

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.470
eight and also centers
the inactive entries.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.850
The target remains in rentals per hour.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.950
No weather, interaction or new
observation has been added.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.530
The fitted weights now operate in
different numerical coordinates.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.060
We save the training statistics and
reuse them at prediction time rather than

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.410
recomputing them for each request batch.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.040
The question is how this changes
optimization under a declared allowance,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.890
while keeping the input information fixed.

00:00:43.108 --> 00:00:47.288
The implementation fits means and
population deviations on training

00:00:47.288 --> 00:00:48.038
features.

00:00:48.608 --> 00:00:51.998
The raw branch instead stores
zero means and unit scales.

00:00:52.648 --> 00:00:55.718
This excerpt calls that
stored raw scaler identity.

00:00:56.368 --> 00:01:00.458
Both paths then use the same
transform and prediction interface.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:04.998
Constant training columns receive
unit scale in the standardized branch,

00:01:05.208 --> 00:01:06.698
preventing division by zero.

00:01:07.288 --> 00:01:09.958
Neither branch fits its
transformation on validation.

00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:14.098
A later request batch cannot change
the meaning of the saved coefficients.

00:01:15.068 --> 00:01:19.988
That fit and predict separation makes
coordinate changes reproducible instead of

00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:22.678
silently refitting the
model when requests arrive.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.290
To compare conditioning,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.170
both paths use full batch SGD at rate
zero point one for two hundred updates.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:38.030
They share half squared error, no penalty
and the same initial prediction function.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.330
We do not give one path a new
optimizer or extra passes.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.570
The parameter arrays are
in different coordinates,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.200
so the same numerical step has different
effects on the represented function.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.350
Raw and standardized gradient norms
also have coordinate dependent units.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:00.310
A lower norm alone is not an
invariant distance between predictors;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.610
training loss and an independent
solve help interpret the trajectory.

00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:08.128
At the fixed allowance,

00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:12.741
raw indicators leave training half
squared error around four thousand,

00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:14.848
one hundred and fourteen point five.

00:02:15.258 --> 00:02:18.185
Standardized coordinates
reach about three thousand,

00:02:18.185 --> 00:02:20.768
one hundred and sixty
seven point five three.

00:02:22.018 --> 00:02:25.748
Later absolute error is also
lower for this standardized fit.

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:28.608
Its final gradient is very small,

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:32.048
but the configured stopping rule
was still the update budget.

00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:36.928
We do not relabel the run as an early
convergence experiment afterward.

00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:40.488
This is evidence of faster
progress under these settings,

00:02:40.758 --> 00:02:44.788
not proof that raw indicators
represent a permanently weaker family.

00:02:47.147 --> 00:02:51.747
A stable training least squares solve
in each coordinate system provides the

00:02:51.747 --> 00:02:52.737
missing comparison.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:56.607
On every observed training
and validation input,

00:02:56.607 --> 00:03:00.217
their forecasts agree within
a few trillionths of a rental.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:04.817
The raw model can represent the same
fitted function on these inputs;

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.797
its two hundred update
result is unfinished.

00:03:08.707 --> 00:03:11.917
Dependent columns mean individual
coefficients can differ.

00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:16.567
Coordinate dependent minimum norm
solutions can also disagree on unsupported

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:17.457
inputs.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.197
We therefore state the checked
prediction agreement precisely.

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:25.367
The result separates numerical
conditioning from the additional feature

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.657
capacity studied in the other families.

00:03:29.817 --> 00:03:33.447
The quiet Monday hour makes
the distinction tangible.

00:03:34.077 --> 00:03:39.117
The raw two hundred step fit predicts
about four point three nine against target

00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:39.787
five.

00:03:40.397 --> 00:03:45.587
The nearly optimized standardized function
predicts minus seventy point six eight.

00:03:46.257 --> 00:03:49.407
The unfinished function is much
closer on that observation,

00:03:49.677 --> 00:03:53.507
despite worse overall training
loss and later absolute error.

00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:57.847
Optimizing the shared objective
moves many rows together;

00:03:58.317 --> 00:04:01.067
it does not promise every
individual row improves.

00:04:01.897 --> 00:04:04.987
Scaling also has not
enforced nonnegative counts.

00:04:05.697 --> 00:04:07.147
Keep the single hour,

00:04:07.237 --> 00:04:11.457
the optimized training quantity and the
later aggregate metric separate when

00:04:11.457 --> 00:04:13.347
explaining why the numbers changed.

